message: "Please cite the manuscript using the preferred citation below."
type: software
title: "The Exact Partially Symmetric Rank of Products of W-States"
authors:
  - given-names: "Wenqi"
    family-names: "Zhu"
    affiliation: "Mathematical Institute, Woodstock Road, University of Oxford, Oxford, UK, OX2 6GG"
    email: "wenqi.zhu@maths.ox.ac.uk"
  - given-names: "Ping"
    family-names: "Nie"
    affiliation: "David R. Cheriton School of Computer Science, University of Waterloo"
    email: "ping.nie@uwaterloo.ca"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/erenup/w-tensor-product-rank"
abstract: >-
  For every k >= 2 and all d_1,...,d_k >= 3, the partially symmetric
  rank over the complex numbers of the product of k generalized W-states,
  represented by the product of the binary forms x_i^(d_i-1) y_i with the
  k symmetric blocks fixed, equals 2^(k-1)(d_1+...+d_k-2k+2). The lower
  bound applies to every complex decomposition; it converts the
  decomposition into weighted points satisfying product moment conditions
  and shows that a weighted bilinear Gram matrix of explicit rational test
  functions is invertible at one finite choice of auxiliary parameters.
  The upper bound is the construction of Canino, Casarotti and
  Santarsiero. More generally, for every k >= 1 and all integers
  a_i >= b_i >= 1, the rank of the product of the binary monomials
  x_i^(a_i) y_i^(b_i), with blocks of degrees a_i+b_i fixed, equals
  (b_1+1)...(b_k+1) plus the sum over i of (a_i-b_i) times the product
  of (b_j+1) over j != i, with a matching explicit finite-character
  decomposition. Includes the paper, plain-text proofs, exact supporting
  checks, and a Lean proof of six universal algebraic components of the
  lower-bound argument and of its one-coordinate case. Files outside paper/ are licensed under MIT; files
  in paper/, including the manuscript source and PDF, are licensed under
  CC BY-SA 4.0.
